class.description:
[FilesManifestServer] keeps [FilesManifest] resources under names. Mods, user content and level editors register a manifest once and then edit it through the server ([method add_folder], [method add_extension], ...), check it with [method validate], save it with [method save_manifest] and get its cached file list with [method get_paths]. Loading the files is done by [method ResourceLoader.load_manifest].
Watching ([method set_watching]) polls the folders of a manifest on the main thread every [member watch_interval] seconds and emits [signal file_added] and [signal file_removed]. It needs no threads and no OS file watchers, so it works the same on all platforms, including the Web export. With a [SceneTree], polling runs automatically; with another [MainLoop], call [method poll] yourself.
Manifests listed in [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/manifests/autoload] are registered on first use of the server. All paths can use the prefixes of [PathPrefixServer]. Use the server from the main thread.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var manifest = FilesManifest.new()
FilesManifestServer.register_manifest("mods", manifest)
FilesManifestServer.add_folder("mods", "user://mods")
FilesManifestServer.add_extension("mods", "tres")
FilesManifestServer.file_added.connect(func(name, path): print("New file: ", path))
FilesManifestServer.set_watching("mods", true)
FilesManifestServer.save_manifest("mods", "user://mods.tres")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var manifest = new FilesManifest();
FilesManifestServer.RegisterManifest("mods", manifest);
FilesManifestServer.AddFolder("mods", "user://mods");
FilesManifestServer.AddExtension("mods", "tres");
FilesManifestServer.Singleton.FileAdded += (name, path) => GD.Print("New file: ", path);
FilesManifestServer.SetWatching("mods", true);
FilesManifestServer.SaveManifest("mods", "user://mods.tres");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
